file session-logs/date/20260906/20260906-154353_the-option-that-silenced-the-collision.kyri put back in the channel, its number corrected before first landing
file session-logs/date/20260906/20260906-160050_the-hypothesis-that-declined-the-sweep.kyri put back in the channel, and told that it died the same death it recovered
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two things want your word rather than another lap. FIRST, reds_fold.sh moves one line of a row and reports verdict=ok: %360 stands on the living pin today at 19 lines and 10 paragraphs, is the largest OPEN row, and is the one most likely to be folded when the pin next fills -- folding it would shelve its heading and leave eighteen lines orphaned, and reds_ledger_monotone would stay green, since a truncated row leaves no gap in 1..N. The repair is small and I can name it exactly: after the row line is dropped, refuse when the following line is neither blank nor a new heading, plus one planted control leg. What holds me off is that the file is shared -- six ships fold rows with it -- and this lap already carries thirteen recovered files, so widening it here would be a second keystone in one round. SECOND, the nineteen peer modules are one line each plus their own witnesses, in four lanes I do not hold. Naming them on the card is what I can do; a sweep across four seats is a word rather than a lap.
